{ Black has played quietly. Can you claim room for your pieces? } 3. d4 { Your two central pawns give your pieces room and challenge his e pawn. [%tail] [%cal Gd2d4] } (3. Bc4 { Also sound. Your bishop develops with an eye on f7. } 3... Nf6 { Also playable. He hits e4 in return, and the center pawns still haven't made their claim. [%cal Bg8f6] }) (3. Nc3 { Also sound. Your knight supports the center before you change the pawns. } 3... c5 { Also playable. He grabs queen-side space of his own before your center pawns even move. [%cal Bc7c5] }) (3. a4 { Playable. You gain space on the wing rather than challenge the center. } 3... Nf6 { Also playable. That wing pawn does nothing for the center, which is still waiting for d4. [%cal Bg8f6] }) (3. h3 { Playable. You prevent a pin, but your central advance can come first. } 3... c5 { Also playable. A slow prophylactic move, while the d pawn is still sitting at home. [%cal Bc7c5] }) 3... exd4 4. Nxd4 4... Nf6 5. Nc3 { Your other knight defends e4 and joins the fight. The e pawn still stands, and your pieces already have all the room they claimed. [%cal Gb1c3] } 1-0


[Event "Capablanca plans: Castle away from the prepared attack"]
[Site "https://lichess.org/analysis/r3k2r/pbpn1p1p/1p2pp2/5q2/2PP4/5N2/P1PQBPPP/R3K2R_w_KQkq_-_1_12"]
