{ Can your knight challenge the bishop that holds his center together? } 10. Ng5 { You attack e6. Trading that bishop will expose his pawn structure. [%cal Gf3g5] } (10. e4 { Also strong. You challenge the center rather than exchange its defender. } 10... Nf6 { Also playable. He develops naturally, and the bishop on e6 is still guarding the center for now. [%cal Bg8f6] }) (10. Qb3 { Also sound. Your queen eyes b3, but it does nothing to challenge the bishop on e6. } 10... Nf6 { Also playable. His knight develops, and the bishop on e6 stands undisturbed. [%cal Bg8f6] }) (10. Qd3 { Also sound. Your queen centralizes on d3, but it does nothing to challenge the bishop on e6. } 10... h6 { Also playable. His pawn advances instead, and the bishop on e6 stands exactly where it was. [%cal Bh7h6] }) (10. a3 { Also sound. Your pawn takes queen-side space, but it does nothing to challenge the bishop on e6. } 10... Nf6 { Also playable. His knight comes out, and the bishop on e6 is still exactly where it was. [%cal Bg8f6] }) (10. Bg5 { Also sound. The bishop develops, but your knight does not challenge e6 yet. } 10... Nge7 { Also playable. His knight defends instead, and the plan to remove the e6 bishop is still one move away. [%cal Bg8e7] }) 10... Nf6 { He develops, but the bishop is still available to exchange. } 11. Nxe6 { You remove the defender. A pawn recapture opens the diagonal from a3. [%cal Gg5e6] } (11. Bf4 { Also sound. Your bishop develops actively, but it leaves the knight's job on e6 undone. } 11... O-O { Also playable. He castles to safety, and the bishop on e6 is still there to be won. [%cal Be8g8] }) (11. Na4 { Also sound. Your knight eyes c5, but it leaves the bishop on e6 alone. } 11... Bb4 { Also playable. His bishop develops actively, and the e6 bishop is still standing too. [%cal Bc5b4] }) (11. a3 { Also sound. Your pawn edges forward on the queen side, but e6 is untouched. } 11... O-O { Also playable. He castles away, and the bishop on e6 remains for the taking. [%cal Be8g8] }) (11. Qb3 { Also sound. Your queen eyes the long diagonal, but it leaves the bishop on e6 untouched. } 11... O-O { Also playable. He tucks his king away, and the bishop on e6 is still sitting there unclaimed. [%cal Be8g8] }) 1-0


[Event "Capablanca plans: Remove the king defender"]
